#: ../../source/start/dev-tools.rst:3
msgid "Installing the developer tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/dev-tools.rst:5
msgid "One command from a fresh clone, and then whichever role you are in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/dev-tools.rst:14
msgid ""
"``make init`` installs everything, which is the right default for a first"
" look around. When you know which part you are working on, the narrower "
"targets are faster:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/start/dev-tools.rst:23
msgid ""
"You also need a Rust toolchain — ``rustup`` with the stable channel. The "
"engine is a Rust crate, so there is no way around it. ``make doctor`` "
"tells you what is installed, what is missing and which target supplies "
"each gap; :doc:`../guides/engine/build` explains the whole arrangement, "
"and :doc:`install` gives the same steps as plain commands for an "
"environment the Makefile knows nothing about."
msgstr ""

